    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Ren §66-s to be §66-u, amd §66-u, Pub Serv L (as proposed in S.1380-A & A.129-A)",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2227\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to requiring gas\ncorporations to file gas safety reports\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.731, to adjust the date the gas safety report is due and add in addi-\ntional items for inclusion in the report.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by aligning the gas safe-\nty report due date with other required quarterly reports; adds leak\nrepair information to the report; and makes other technical changes to\nclarify responsibilities of the Public Service Commission.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 52 of the laws of 2022, this legislation is a\nnegotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to chapter 731 of the Laws of 2022. S.1380A and A.129A\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the public service law relating to\nfiling gas safety reports, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n1380-A and A. 129-A, takes effect.\n",
